            <div type="edition" xml:space="preserve">
                <ab xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"><lb n="1"/>to-i te-o-i | to u-la-ta-i | o-na-si-wo-i-ko-se | o sa-ta-si-wo-i-<lb n="2"/>ko-ne ka-te-se-ta-se | e-u-ko-la | i tu-ka-i</ab>
            </div>
            <div type="translation" xml:lang="DE" resp="Klaus Hallof"><ab xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"><lb n="1"/>Dem Gott Hylatas hat Onasiwoikos S.d. Stasiwoi-<lb n="2"/>kos, (dies) geweiht wegen des Gelübdes, zum Heil.</ab></div><div type="translation" xml:lang="GRC" resp=" "><ab xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0"><lb n="1"/>τῶι θεῶι τῷ Ὑλάται Ὀνασίϝοικος ὁ Στασιϝοί‒<lb n="2"/>κων κατέστασε εὐχωλᾷ ἰ(ν) τύχαι.</ab></div>
            <div type="bibliography">
